# 18. 面试速答

### What is pre-training?

> **Pre-training is the first large-scale training stage where a model learns broad language, knowledge, and other patterns from massive datasets using objectives such as next-token prediction or denoising.**

### What is post-training?

> **Post-training further trains a pretrained base model on smaller, higher-quality or preference-oriented data to improve instruction following, helpfulness, alignment, safety, or task-specific behavior.**

### Why can next-token prediction learn useful representations?

> **Although the objective is simple, accurately predicting the next token across diverse data requires the model to capture grammar, semantics, world knowledge, context, and recurring reasoning and programming patterns.**

### What is span corruption?

> **Span corruption removes spans from the input and asks an encoder-decoder model to reconstruct the missing text. The encoder processes the corrupted context, while the decoder autoregressively generates the missing spans.**

### Prefix Prediction vs Span Corruption?

> **Prefix prediction encodes the beginning of a sequence and generates its continuation, while span corruption removes pieces throughout the sequence and reconstructs them using surrounding context.**

# 19. 一句话总结

> **Pre-training uses a scalable prediction objective on massive data to learn broad capabilities; post-training shapes the pretrained model toward desired behavior. For encoder-decoder models, prefix-to-suffix prediction and span corruption construct different input-target pairs, but both can train the decoder using the same token-level cross-entropy loss.**
